.TH THEME 6
.SH NAME
theme \- colours for rio, acme, menus and libcontrol programs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B $home/lib/theme
.br
.B /lib/theme
.SH DESCRIPTION
A theme names colours.
Programs read the first of
.B $home/lib/theme
and
.B /lib/theme
that exists, once, when they start;
a name the theme does not give keeps the program's own colour,
so with no theme everything looks as it always has.
.PP
Each line is a name, then its colours, separated by blanks:
.IP
.EX
back	ffffff
tag	fg=000000 bg=eaffff
keyword	fg=0000aa
.EE
.PP
A colour is six hexadecimal digits,
.IR rrggbb ,
with or without a leading
.LR # .
A bare colour is the name's one colour;
.BI fg= colour
and
.BI bg= colour
give text and background.
A name starts with a letter; a line that starts with
.L #
is a comment, and words a program does not know are ignored.
A later line for a name replaces an earlier one.
This is the format of 9front's rio themes, so their files serve as they are.
.PP
.IR Acme 's
per-window
.B style
file (see
.IR acme (4))
has the same lines, followed by runs:
.IP
.EX
keyword	fg=aa0000
0 6 keyword
12 20 comment
.EE
.PP
A run is a line of three fields: its start and length in runes, and a name.
A run whose name the window has not given takes the theme's colours,
so a program that marks text names roles and the theme chooses how they look.
For these a bare colour is the text's.
.SS Names
.TP
.I rio
.BR back ,
.BR text ,
.BR high ,
.BR htext
and
.B border
for the windows' text;
.B title
and
.B ltitle
for the current window's border and the others',
.BR hold ,
.B lhold
and
.B palehold
for those in hold mode,
.B size
for the outline as a window is swept, and
.B rioback
for the background.
.TP
menus
.BR menuback ,
.BR menuhigh ,
.BR menubord ,
.B menutext
and
.BR menuhtext ,
for
.IR menuhit (2)
in every program.
.TP
.I acme
.B tag
and
.B body
for text and background,
.B tagsel
and
.B bodysel
for selections,
.B tagborder
and
.BR bodyborder ;
.B modbutton
and
.B colbutton
for the boxes at the left of tags, and
.B but2
and
.B but3
for text swept with buttons 2 and 3.
For
.BR tag ,
.BR tagsel ,
.B body
and
.BR bodysel ,
a bare colour is the background.
.TP
.IR control (2)
.BR back ,
.BR text ,
.BR border ,
.BR high ,
.BR pale ,
.B entry
and
.BR ok ,
which controls take when not told otherwise, and which programs such as
.I auth/fgui
(see
.IR factotum (4))
name.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/libdraw/theme.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR rio (1),
.IR acme (1),
.IR acme (4),
.IR control (2),
.IR color (6)
.br
